items.text:
I gave it a year or so to cook some more and came back to the game. The game runs better, and many of the bugs I was facing in my last play-through are gone. Better doesn't always mean well, but it is improving. After more than quadrupling my previous playtime, I have to say it is worth the price of admission now. I understand actual contentand things to do still do tend to dry up after a bit, but the game itself is definitely improved.



Old Review Below
{Spent days building a ship out of wreckage, paid the entire debt on it. Saved out with zero debt. Launched the save, owed a million $ (in past due payments somehow) in debt on a ship worth 1.5mil preventing me from undocking. Sold the ship to pay the debt as that was the only way to move forward and now am given the choice of assume a new debt on a new ship or not playing. I choose to uninstall.}

items.text_zh:
我给了它一年左右的时间再打磨打磨，然后回到了这款游戏。游戏运行得更好了，我上次游玩时遇到的许多bug都消失了。更好并不总是意味着好，但它确实在改进。在把之前的游玩时间翻了两番还多之后，我不得不说现在它值这个票价了。我明白实际内容和可做的事情过一阵子确实还是会枯竭，但游戏本身绝对改进了。



以下是旧评测
{花了好几天用残骸造了一艘飞船，还清了它身上的全部债务。存档时零债务。加载存档后，却欠了一百万美元（不知怎么变成了逾期付款）的债务，而飞船价值150万，这让我无法脱离对接。我卖掉了飞船来还债，因为那是唯一能继续前进的办法，而现在我面临的选择是：在一艘新飞船上承担新债务，或者不玩。我选择卸载。}
